WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.540
You might not recognize Amber Heard as Mera
in Aquaman.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.660
That bright red hair isn't her usual look,
for one thing.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.260
Most of the time she's blonde, and looks much
less like a warrior mermaid.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.820
Let's take a look at the major stepping stones
in Amber Heard's career.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.160
Heard was still in her teens when North Country
came out in 2005, and she wasn't featured

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.840
in any of the ads or trailers.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.260
The focus of the film was Charlize Theron,
who plays Josey Aimes, a female iron miner

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.100
who takes a stand against sexual harassment.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.040
A young Amber Heard plays the teenage Josey
in some disturbing flashbacks.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.240
Heard makes an impression here, despite her
lack of screentime.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.640
She looks enough like Charlize Theron to believably
play a younger version of the same character,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.230
but she's also already a strong actress in
her own right, delivering an effective performance

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.940
in some difficult-to-watch scenes.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:54.800
Heard was the female lead in Hidden Palms,
a 2007 CW series from Kevin Williamson, creator

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.780
of Dawson's Creek.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.640
The show was a teen drama about dark secrets
lurking underneath the sun-drenched surface

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.720
of an affluent Palm Springs neighborhood.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.060
Heard played Greta, the mysterious girl next
door who's immediately fascinating to the

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.940
series lead, but who's also at the center
of several local mysteries.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.860
The series received a summer order of eight
initial episodes, and was canceled due to

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.860
low ratings by the time all eight had aired.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.180
It's largely forgotten today, but it did raise
Amber Heard's profile enough to help her launch

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:27.050
her film career, which no doubt benefited
from this show ending too soon for her to

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:27.540
be tied to it.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.280
Never Back Down was a teen movie about mixed
martial arts fighting, which probably seemed

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.090
like a really good idea in 2008.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.840
"Those look kind of cute on you."

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.420
"Eww...

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:40.760
They're still sweaty."

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.480
It's an extremely by-the-book plot, in which
a teenage boy at a new school must learn to

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.870
be the best MMA fighter in order to defeat
a bully and prove himself to all the other

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:50.360
kids.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.220
However, Amber Heard had plenty to do as the
female lead of the movie.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.860
She starts out as the girlfriend of the MMA-fighting
bully, who tricks the protagonist into a fight

00:01:58.860 --> 00:01:59.740
he's not ready for.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:05.380
Even in a largely unmemorable movie, it was
a showy role for a young actress like Heard,

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.680
and it helped launch her into bigger and better
parts.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:12.280
Pineapple Express, coming right on the heels
of Never Back Down, was the movie that really

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.800
made Amber Heard a star.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:19.360
She plays a high school senior in an ill-advised
relationship with the movie's stoner process

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.340
server hero, played by Seth Rogen.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:26.880
Produced by Judd Apatow and directed by indie
darling David Gordon Green, Pineapple Express

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.260
was both a hit and a much-discussed comedy
of 2008.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.220
Rogen and co-star James Franco were already
big stars, but it took at least three people's

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:40.340
careers to the next level: Green himself,
supporting player Danny McBride, and of course

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.140
rising ingenue Amber Heard.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:49.020
Heard had only one scene in the 2009 post-apocalyptic
horror comedy Zombieland, but it was one of

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.160
the most memorable in the movie.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.530
Jesse Eisenberg's Columbus explains how he
became aware of the zombie plague when his

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.860
attractive next door neighbor, played by Heard,
sought refuge in his apartment after being

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.900
attacked by what she thought was a crazed
homeless man trying to bite her.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.020
Naturally, Eisenberg wakes the next morning
to find that Heard has become a zombie.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:10.580
The whole point of her character here is that
she's a basic hot girl who turns into a monster,

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.540
but Heard still somehow takes that premise
and makes it charming, and pretty scary:

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.480
In 2011 Heard returned to TV, but found no
more success this time around than she did

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.380
with Hidden Palms.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:29.040
The Playboy Club was at least splashier to
start with, a historical drama for NBC about

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.080
the women working at the original Playboy
Club in 1961 Chicago.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:37.660
Heard played Maureen, a young woman who becomes
a Playboy Bunny shortly after arriving in

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.400
the city on the run from a dark past.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:44.260
The nature of Maureen's past was never explored,
as it turns out, because The Playboy Club

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.660
was cancelled after only three episodes.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.680
The Rum Diary is another example of Heard
taking a pretty typical "hot girl" part and

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.690
making it her own.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:57.690
This 2011 film by Bruce Robinson was based
on a Hunter S. Thompson book and stars Johnny

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:01.769
Depp as a down-on-his-luck writer who takes
a job in San Juan, Puerto Rico during the

00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:02.940
early 1960s.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.080
Heard plays a girl he meets while he's in
a boat and she's skinny-dipping, and she goes

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.989
off to become the center of a love triangle
between him and a shady realtor played by

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:11.640
Aaron Eckhart.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:16.900
The Rum Diary is how Heard and Depp first
met, leading to a relationship that started

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:23.199
in 2012, became a marriage in 2015, and ended
in 2016 with Heard filing for divorce and

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.000
accusing Depp of domestic abuse.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.960
All the Boys Love Mandy Lane is a slasher-style
horror movie about an unusual high school

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.520
girl, and the secrets she does her best to
keep as the other teens around her start dying.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.400
Heard played the title role, and it might
have been her breakout part if the movie had

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.540
come out as originally planned.

00:04:40.969 --> 00:04:46.580
It was filmed in 2006, before almost everything
else on this list, with a 20-year-old Heard

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.620
perfectly cast as the mysterious Mandy.

00:04:49.069 --> 00:04:52.999
Unfortunately, the Weinstein Company declined
to distribute it, and the company they handed

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.660
it off to went out of business.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:59.020
The movie went unreleased in the United States
for seven years, before finally coming out

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:03.620
on video in 2013, after Amber Heard was enough
of a star to get people to watch it.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:09.360
The sequel to 2010's Machete was not a success
at the box office or among critics, but it

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.159
was the kind of sequel that made sense for
the over-the-top character played by Danny

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.520
Trejo and the unique sensibility of director
Robert Rodriguez.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.280
The supporting cast of Machete Kills features
a parade of beautiful women.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.560
Amber Heard is still a standout, however.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.560
She plays Blanca Vasquez, a beauty queen who's
also a secret agent and Machete's handler

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.780
on his mission to stop a madman from launching
a nuclear missile at Washington, D.C.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:37.940
Interestingly, Amber Heard plays a glamorous
government assassin again in 2014's 3 Days

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.770
To Kill, but in a slightly less outrageous
context.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:45.920
The film stars Kevin Costner as a veteran
CIA agent with an estranged family and terminal

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:46.420
cancer.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.640
Heard's younger and more ruthless agent is
tasked with manipulating him into hunting

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.789
down one last target by offering him an experimental
cure for his illness.

00:05:54.789 --> 00:05:59.449
3 Days To Kill is one of those "Aging Baby
Boomer" action movies, where an older man

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:02.080
proves that he still has what it takes to
get the job done.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:06.780
Thankfully, unlike some movies of this type,
the protagonist's focus remains on his family,

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.000
meaning that Heard is never asked to be a
May/December love interest for Costner.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:17.139
2015's Magic Mike XXL was a phenomenon, far
more so than the original Magic Mike.

00:06:17.139 --> 00:06:22.600
The first movie was a drama about male strippers,
whereas the sequel was a feel-good celebration

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.919
of male strippers, which unsurprisingly made
it a huge hit among women, as well as gay

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:30.740
men and pretty much anyone who's comfortable
watching muscular men dance with their shirts

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:31.240
off.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.520
Amber Heard was one of many fresh cast members
to join for the sequel, playing a new love

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.840
interest for Magic Mike, played by Channing
Tatum.

00:06:38.309 --> 00:06:42.460
At first her photographer character seems
likely to be a one-night stand, but after

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:46.939
she and Mike mutually decide not to have sex,
she shows back up later in the movie and they

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.360
build more of a relationship.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.520
One thing that's clear in looking back at
Amber Heard's career so far is that she's

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.080
obviously been chosen for many roles because
of how beautiful she is.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:07:00.460
However, as we've seen again and again, what
makes her interesting in those roles is the

00:07:00.469 --> 00:07:05.129
intelligence she always displays, adding depth
to characters who weren't necessarily created

00:07:05.129 --> 00:07:05.620
to have any.

